  "span_note": "Truncated to a 2-day window (2023-11-20 to 2023-11-21, R=565 rolling origins) instead of the full 21-day span used by the contemporaneous W1 study (brussels_xlstm_bottleneck_residual_corr_timeresolved.json, R=6037), because of a rebuttal deadline. The full 21-day run was started and killed after 1/21 chunks (~1hr projected total) to get a result in time. This shortens the effective sample size per lag bin (T ~ 560 vs ~6000) but the qualitative decay pattern -- contemporaneous correlation ~0.40, decaying smoothly and staying well above the independence floor through lag=30min -- is unambiguous even at this T. Re-running the full 21-day span (python src/curvature_cross_lag_residual_corr.py --span_start 2023-11-20 --span_end 2023-12-10 --device 1, ~1hr) would tighten the error bars but is not expected to change the qualitative conclusion."
